  "line": 373,
  "title": "Redacting the whole run state on every save changes what a resumed run executes and compares",
  "detail": "`save()` now persists `redactGateData(this.state)` while the live state stays as it was, so a resumed run reads altered inputs. `gatesConfig`, `baselineScripts`, spec, holdout, feedback and answers all go through credential replacement and VT-control stripping. Reproduced with a temporary engine test: a gate command containing a registered synthetic credential, and separately one containing a literal ESC[31m, each went from \"uninterrupted: succeeded\" to \"restarted: needs_human\", with a blocking `regressed` gate and altered-command output. An unchanged script became a blocking `gate-script-changed` finding, and sanitized holdout steps changed a gate substitution from `blocked` to `met`. The persisted baseline cache entry also stops satisfying `cacheableBaseline`'s exact-command comparison. That is the earlier \"redacted data is executed\" finding in a new place, since the handle now correctly carries only an identity. None of the seven fixes needed it, and it adds an extra stringify and parse to every save: a 12.7 MB synthetic state went from 8.86 ms to 17.78 ms per save. Fix: revert the whole-state redaction. Redact gate results and output where they are stored or shown (artifacts, events, `lastGates`, the baseline artifact), as main already does, and leave the configuration the engine executes or compares literally untouched. Test: the credential and escape-character commands give the same verdict uninterrupted and after a restart at `gate-started`."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/gates/executor.ts",
  "line": 166,
  "title": "Local gate work can keep running after its execution is forgotten",
  "detail": "Two paths drop an execution without stopping it. (1) `executeGate` awaits `Promise.all([execution.result, events])`. If a hook called while forwarding events throws (a land-log write, say), the promise rejects, the `finally` neither cancels nor awaits the execution, and `runGateExecution` (gate-execution.ts:62) then clears the handle. Reproduced: a hook threw `log write failed` after the first check, a replacement execution completed, and the original check (`sleep 900`) kept running. (2) gate-execution.ts:29 discards a stored handle for another purpose or SHA with only a save. When that execution is still live in this process, it keeps running too. Normal shutdown cancellation does work, but discarding isn't cancelling. Fix: before forgetting an execution, whether by error, discard or settle, cancel it and await its end. Make a hook failure cancel the execution and surface as the stage's error, so it can't leave a result behind. Test: a throwing hook, and a discarded live handle, each leave no running child (check by the pid the test started) and no occupied gate slot."
 },
